1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Welche Kontakte hatten Sie vor dem 7. Oktober zu Menschen aus Gaza?

2
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:16,433
Many people here had a good relationship

3
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:19,400
with people from Gaza.

4
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:21,466
People don’t know this, but

5
00:00:21,533 --> 00:00:23,366
life is stronger than everything.

6
00:00:23,766 --> 00:00:25,833
And we are very close.

7
00:00:25,833 --> 00:00:28,966
This is like half a mile,

8
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:35,033
the distance is about half a mile,

9
00:00:35,033 --> 00:00:38,433
and my husband

10
00:00:38,433 --> 00:00:42,033
used to be the manager of two dairy farms here.

11
00:00:42,033 --> 00:00:43,833
Today he's only the manager of one,

12
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:46,666
but his dairy farms were all...

13
00:00:46,966 --> 00:00:50,100
he's a very good professional in what he does,

14
00:00:50,100 --> 00:00:53,933
so many merchants from Gaza used to have

15
00:00:53,933 --> 00:00:58,200
working relationships with him and

16
00:00:58,200 --> 00:01:01,366
because they came to buy things,

17
00:01:01,966 --> 00:01:03,466
and sell things,

18
00:01:03,466 --> 00:01:06,933
and with many of them,

19
00:01:06,933 --> 00:01:10,166
friendships developed.

20
00:01:10,166 --> 00:01:13,366
I had Gazans at my wedding here, at the kibbutz.

21
00:01:13,866 --> 00:01:16,366
I had Gazans at my dinner table.

22
00:01:17,833 --> 00:01:18,966
More than once.

23
00:01:19,533 --> 00:01:23,733
And when I studied

24
00:01:23,866 --> 00:01:26,333
Middle Eastern studies in Tel Aviv University,

25
00:01:26,333 --> 00:01:29,333
and I wanted to research about the

26
00:01:30,066 --> 00:01:33,366
economic policy of Hamas

27
00:01:33,533 --> 00:01:40,233
I interviewed merchants from Gaza in my living room.

28
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:42,666
So yes,

29
00:01:42,666 --> 00:01:46,066
we had a very close relationship with them.

30
00:01:46,566 --> 00:01:48,266
Up until October 7.

